    "problem": "Statement is faithful. Let $f$ be a surjective block code from a mixing sofic shift $T$ to itself. When does there exist an SFT $T'\\supset T$ such that $f(T')\\subset T$? (Boyle 2008, Problem 16.3.)",
    "status_literature": "- **Open.** Same circle as 16.2. The existence of an ambient SFT into which a given surjective endomorphism of a sofic shift extends remains unresolved; Boyle's papers on closed extensions and \"good\" covers provide examples but no general characterization.",
